{"name":"Craft","hex":"#293b4a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Craft","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Craft"}],"entries":[{"title":"Craft","blocks":[{"text":"A craft or trade is a pastime or an occupation that requires particular skills and knowledge of skilled work. In a historical sense, particularly the Middle Ages and earlier, the term is usually applied to people occupied in small scale production of goods, or their maintenance, for example by tinkers. The traditional term craftsman is nowadays often replaced by artisan and by craftsperson."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Craft_fair_and_folk_festival_Bangladesh_2024_at_Sonargaon_museum_35.jpg/330px-Craft_fair_and_folk_festival_Bangladesh_2024_at_Sonargaon_museum_35.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Craft"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Swanson_Shoe_Repair_18.jpg/500px-Swanson_Shoe_Repair_18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Swanson_Shoe_Repair_18.jpg/1280px-Swanson_Shoe_Repair_18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Swanson_Shoe_Repair_18.jpg/500px-Swanson_Shoe_Repair_18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Shoes are repaired by a skilled shoemaker; here he evaluates a pair of shoes with a customer watching.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASwanson_Shoe_Repair_18.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/NSRW_Japanese_potter_at_his_wheel.jpg/500px-NSRW_Japanese_potter_at_his_wheel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x